WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.440
Feifei: Hello, this The English We Speak.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.400
I'm Feifei...

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.800
Rob: ...and don't you know who I am?!

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.980
I am Rob.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.200
Feifei: Yes, we all know that, Rob.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.680
Rob: But I am THE Rob - Rob of

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.480
The English We Speak.

00:00:19.482 --> 00:00:21.370
There is nobody else like me.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.030
Feifei: Yeah, yeah, yeah - don't milk it!

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.820
Rob: Eh? Come on, show me

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.295
some respect. Ouch, I seem to have

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.980
pulled a muscle - ooo, that hurts.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.380
Feifei: Come on, Rob. You hardly moved.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.460
Rob: Ouch, it's in my lower back. It's so

00:00:36.478 --> 00:00:39.490
painful, I don't know if I can carry on.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.870
Feifei: You are milking it again!

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.300
Rob: Feifei - what am I 'milking' exactly?

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.720
Feifei: Everything! 'To milk it' means to

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.720
take full advantage of a situation usually

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.840
to gain sympathy, respect or kindness.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.277
Sometimes, like Rob, you fake something

00:00:56.277 --> 00:00:57.440
to get attention

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.450
- that's when we say 'You're milking it'.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.110
Rob: Are you talking about me?

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.940
Feifei: Of course I am, Rob. Let's hear

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:05.460
some examples of

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.380
other people 'milking it'...

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.220
OK, don't milk it, Sam! You've told me

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.860
a hundred times you've got tickets

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.860
for the World Cup final.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.200
Tom's had a week off work with a cold -

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.060
I think he's milking it now.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.340
Since her promotion, Freya keeps

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.111
bossing us around and telling us

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.880
to call her 'Miss Brown'

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.740
- she's really milking it!

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.140
Feifei: You're listening to The English

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.340
We Speak from BBC Learning English,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.080
and we're talking about the phrase

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.940
'to milk it'. This means to take

00:01:40.947 --> 00:01:43.600
full advantage of a situation

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.920
usually to gain sympathy, respect

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.660
or kindness. So Rob, have you got

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.140
what 'milking it' means?

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.480
Rob: I do, and I seemed to have recovered

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:55.480
from pulled muscle but I've become so...

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.420
thirsty, I was wondering...

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.340
Feifei: ...if I could get you a drink of milk?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.460
Rob: No, Feifei. I was thinking of

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.100
a cup of coffee. You are so very kind

00:02:05.101 --> 00:02:05.979
and generous.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.060
Feifei: You are milking it again, Rob.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.100
Actually, I've got just the thing for you.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.920
Hold on...

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.340
Meet Daisy!

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:20.560
Daisy: Moo... moo...

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.780
Rob: A cow!!! How do I milk that?

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:26.160
Feifei: I'd start down there somewhere.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.520
Good luck.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.760
Rob: Bye.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:32.620
Daisy: Moo... moo...

